## Key Learnings

* SOC detection is architecture-dependent: ingestion reliability, storage governance, and integrity controls matter as much as detection logic
* Context enrichment (identity/asset baselines/history) is the main false-positive reducer and must exist as a first-class layer
* Telemetry pipelines are adversarial targets; blinding, tampering, poisoning, and alert flooding must be explicitly threat-modeled
* Vendor-neutral design can be mapped cleanly to cloud services when the system boundaries, control placement, and workflow are correct
* Strong detection systems require governance + feedback loops; without them, baseline and rule logic decays over time

